markdown <<MARKDOWN
## For vs. While: When to Use Each

<div style="background-color: #D5EFFF; border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #06338D; line-height: 1.6;">
    <strong>&#128161; The rule of thumb to give students:</strong> use a for loop when you know the number of repetitions in advance, the Going Viral simulation ran for a set number of days. Use a while loop when you're repeating until something becomes true, and you don't know ahead of time how many repetitions that'll take, the Time to 10 Million simulation ran until a target was hit. Same underlying idea, repetition, two different ways of deciding when to stop.
  </div>
</div>

<hr>

